    return_value=ToolOk(
        is_error=False,
        output="     1\t# Quota Implementation Guide\n     2\t\n     3\tThis gui
de is the backend contract for adding or changing quota-protected\n     4\tYalla
Control Plane behavior. It applies to API-backed resource creation,\n     5\tdur
able provisioning requests, metered usage, and any repository service that\n    
6\tmust prevent a tenant from exceeding plan or organization limits.\n     7\t\n
    8\tThe request path remains:\n     9\t\n    10\t```text\n    11\tCustomer / 
Agent / CI\n    12\t  -> Yalla Control Plane API\n    13\t  -> Postgres source o
f truth\n    14\t  -> worker\n    15\t  -> private Dokploy API\n    16\t```\n   
17\t\n    18\tShort form: Yalla API -> Postgres source of truth -> worker -> pri
vate Dokploy API.\n    19\t\n    20\tDo not expose raw Dokploy operations from q
uota code. Do not call Dokploy from\n    21\tquota code. The quota layer protect
s Yalla source-of-truth writes; workers call\n    22\ttyped Dokploy clients only
after auth, policy, idempotency, quota, audit, and\n    23\tdesired-state persis
tence have succeeded.\n    24\t\n    25\t## Add or change quota enforcement\n   
26\t\n    27\t1. Define the contract first: protected resource, `policy.Action`,
quota\n    28\t   dimension, enforcement mode, stable error code, audit event, i
dempotency\n    29\t   behavior, and compatibility impact.\n    30\t2. Use the c
losed `store.QuotaResource` set for the dimension. Adding a new\n    31\t   dime
nsion requires a migration for the `quota_resource` domain, a Go\n    32\t   con
stant in `internal/controlplane/store`, membership in the `Valid` map,\n    33\t
  and tests that prove the value is accepted end to end.\n    34\t3. Keep quota 
policy and usage data in `internal/controlplane/store`.\n    35\t   Repository-b
acked services should depend on the `store.QuotaReserver` port,\n    36\t   whil
e production wiring uses `quota.Checker` from `internal/controlplane/quota`.\n  
 37\t4. Call `Reserve` for count-based dimensions and `ReserveAmount` for magnit
ude\n    38\t   dimensions such as CPU, memory, storage, deployment counts, or u
sage-derived\n    39\t   allocations.\n    40\t5. Quota reservations happen in t
he same transaction as the desired-state write.\n    41\t   Use `Store.Write` so
the quota check, `quota_reservations` insert, source\n    42\t   row mutation, i
dempotency row, audit row, and job enqueue commit or roll back\n    43\t   toget
her.\n    44\t6. Every customer-data query must be tenant-scoped by `organizatio
n_id` or a\n    45\t   verified parent join. Unknown and cross-tenant IDs must c
ollapse to typed\n    46\t   not-found behavior rather than leaking another tena
nt's existence.\n    47\t7. Return quota failures through `apierr.QuotaExceeded`
. The wrapped\n    48\t   `quota.ExceededDetail` is recoverable with `quota.Deta
ilOf` and carries only\n    49\t   bounded counters: resource, current, reserved
, requested, and limit.\n    50\t8. Emit quota decision telemetry through `telem
etry.QuotaUsageMetrics`. Keep\n    51\t   labels low-cardinality; request, corre
lation, organization, principal, and\n    52\t   job identifiers are incident hi
nts only.\n    53\t9. Keep handlers thin. HTTP routes authorize with the exact `
policy.Action`,\n    54\t   delegate to repository-backed services, and render s
table JSON envelopes.\n    55\t10. Normal tests use fake Dokploy or no Dokploy d
ependency. Live Dokploy smoke\n    56\t    tests are explicitly external and mus
t never be part of quota validation.\n    57\t\n    58\t## Data model\n    59\t\
n    60\tQuota implementation pivots on these source-of-truth tables and types:\
n    61\t\n    62\t- `quota_policies`: effective hard, soft, metered, or disable
d limits by plan\n    63\t  or organization override.\n    64\t- `usage_counters
`: current usage that is locked for hard-limit decisions.\n    65\t- `quota_rese
rvations`: active and settled reservations that bridge the quota\n    66\t  deci
sion to the resource mutation.\n    67\t- `quota_reservation_events`: audited st
ate-machine events for reservation\n    68\t  lifecycle changes.\n    69\t- `sto
re.QuotaRepository`: the repository that resolves limits, locks usage,\n    70\t
 sums active reservations, inserts reservations, and transitions lifecycle\n    
71\t  state.\n    72\t- `store.QuotaReserver`: the service port used by reposito
ry services so quota\n    73\t  enforcement stays testable.\n    74\t- `quota.Ch
ecker`: the production quota checker service that implements the\n    75\t  port
using `store.QuotaRepository`.\n    76\t\n    77\tHard-limit rejection must happ
en before a resource row, provisioning job, or\n    78\tDokploy mutation is comm
itted. soft-limit warnings are allowed to proceed but\n    79\tmust be surfaced 
as structured `yalla.output.v1.warnings`, not as ad hoc\n    80\tresponse fields
. Metered limits record usage for billing and review without a\n    81\tceiling.
Disabled limits do not reserve.\n    82\t\n    83\t## Stable outputs\n    84\t\n
   85\tAll public HTTP responses above quota code use stable JSON envelopes:\n  
 86\t\n    87\t```yaml\n    88\tschema_version: yalla.output.v1\n    89\tok: tru
e\n    90\trequest_id: req_example\n    91\tdata:\n    92\t  id: resource_exampl
e\n    93\t```\n    94\t\n    95\tQuota rejections use the stable error envelope
and HTTP 429:\n    96\t\n    97\t```yaml\n    98\tschema_version: yalla.error.v1
\n    99\tok: false\n   100\trequest_id: req_example\n   101\terror:\n   102\t  
code: E_QUOTA_EXCEEDED\n   103\t  message: quota exceeded\n   104\t  docs_url: h
ttps://docs.yalla.example/errors/E_QUOTA_EXCEEDED\n   105\t```\n   106\t\n   107
\tDo not expose raw counters from another tenant. Only return quota details afte
r\n   108\tauth and policy have already established the caller can act on the sc
oped\n   109\torganization.\n   110\t\n   111\t## Required environment variables
\n   112\t\n   113\tThis section lists the required environment variables for lo
cal quota\n   114\tverification.\n   115\t\n   116\tMost quota unit tests use fa
kes and need no external services. Persistence,\n   117\ttenant-isolation, and c
oncurrency tests require an isolated local Postgres base\n   118\tDSN:\n   119\t
\n   120\t```bash\n   121\texport YALLA_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<redacted:postgres-pas
sword>\n   122\tdocker compose up -d postgres\n   123\tdocker compose ps postgre
s\n   124\texport YALLA_TEST_DATABASE_URL=<redacted:postgres-dsn>\n   125\t```\n
  126\t\n   127\texpected output: the `postgres` service reports a healthy statu
s, and Go test\n   128\tpackages with runnable tests end in `ok`. When the datab
ase variable is not\n   129\tconfigured, expected output includes\n   130\t`YALL
A_TEST_DATABASE_URL not set; skipping Postgres integration test`.\n   131\t\n   
132\tLive Dokploy credentials are not required for quota work. The only allowed 
live\n   133\tsmoke remains explicit and external:\n   134\t\n   135\t```bash\n 
 136\tYALLA_EXTERNAL_DOKPLOY=1 go test -run TestLiveDokploySmoke ./...\n   137\t
```\n   138\t\n   139\tThat command must never run against production.\n   140\t
\n   141\t## Verification commands\n   142\t\n   143\tRun focused quota checks w
hile developing:\n   144\t\n   145\t```bash\n   146\tgo test ./internal/controlp
lane/quota/...\n   147\tgo test ./internal/controlplane/store/...\n   148\tgo te
st -run TestQuotaConcurrency ./...\n   149\tgo test -run TestPolicyMatrix ./...\
n   150\tgo test -run TestTenantIsolation ./...\n   151\t```\n   152\t\n   153\t
Run the full required pre-commit gate before marking a quota story complete:\n  
154\t\n   155\t```bash\n   156\tgofmt -w .\n   157\tgoimports -w .\n   158\tgo m
od tidy\n   159\tgo test ./...\n   160\tgo test -race ./...\n   161\tgo vet ./..
.\n   162\tscripts/verify.sh\n   163\t```\n   164\t\n   165\tThe release gate fo
