569\t## TLS and proxy header trust (BE-0356)\n   570\t\n   571\t`http_server_har
dening_static_test.go` pins the operator-facing\n   572\tcontract that (a) the A
PI binary does not terminate TLS itself and\n   573\t(b) the rate limiter trusts
only a closed set of forwarded-IP\n   574\theaders. Three real-file matchers run
alongside one synthetic\n   575\tself-check (`TestHTTPServerHardeningStaticAnaly
zerDetectsRegressions`):\n   576\t\n   577\t- **`cmd/yalla-api/main.go`** — `fin
dAPITLSRegressions` walks the\n   578\t  AST and rejects: (1) any call whose sel
ector name is in\n   579\t  `forbiddenAPITLSCallSelectors` (`ListenAndServeTLS`,
`ServeTLS`),\n   580\t  regardless of receiver; (2) any `http.Server` composite 
literal\n   581\t  that omits a field from `requiredHTTPServerFields`\n   582\t 
(`ReadHeaderTimeout` is the Slowloris guard) OR contains a field\n   583\t  from
`forbiddenAPITLSStructFields` (`TLSConfig`, `TLSNextProto`);\n   584\t  (3) any 
assignment whose LHS selector is in\n   585\t  `forbiddenAPITLSStructFields` (th
e post-construction mutation\n   586\t  seam). The matcher uses the package-qual
ified type selector\n   587\t  `http.Server`, so unrelated structs in `main.go` 
are not scanned.\n   588\t- **`internal/controlplane/httpapi/ratelimit.go`** —\n
  589\t  `findProxyHeaderTrustRegressions` runs two passes. The scoped\n   590\t
 pass locates the `ClientIP` function by name and walks every\n   591\t  `*.Head
er.Get("...")` inside it; any literal not in\n   592\t  `allowedProxyHeaderLiter
als` (`X-Forwarded-For`, `X-Real-IP`,\n   593\t  case-sensitive) is flagged. The
scoped pass also asserts the\n   594\t  body references `RemoteAddr` so the fall
back chain stays intact.\n   595\t  The file-wide pass walks every string litera
l in the file and\n   596\t  flags any whose lower-cased form is in\n   597\t  `
forbiddenProxyHeaderLiterals` (RFC 7239 `Forwarded`,\n   598\t  `True-Client-IP`
, `CF-Connecting-IP`, `Fastly-Client-IP`,\n   599\t  `X-Client-IP`, `X-Forwarded
-{Host,Proto,Server,Port}`,\n   600\t  `X-Original-Forwarded-For`). If `ClientIP
` is missing entirely\n   601\t  the matcher emits a single "missing function" h
it so the gate\n   602\t  cannot pass silently when its target is removed.\n   6
03\t- **`SECURITY.md`** —\n   604\t  `TestHTTPServerHardeningSecurityDocumentsTL
SAndProxyTrust` pins\n   605\t  the `## TLS Termination and Proxy Header Trust` 
heading, the\n   606\t  verification-gates table row, and the canonical substrin
gs\n   607\t  (`TLS is terminated at the operator\'s reverse proxy`,\n   608\t  
`ReadHeaderTimeout`, `X-Forwarded-For`, `X-Real-IP`, and the\n   609\t  test fil
e path itself). The substrings carry the load-bearing\n   610\t  facts so a futu
re reader does not have to open the test file to\n   611\t  learn the contract.\
n   612\t\n   613\tWhen adding or removing a trusted forwarding header, update\n
  614\t`allowedProxyHeaderLiterals` AND the `ClientIP` body AND the\n   615\tSEC
URITY.md section in the same edit. When adding or removing a\n   616\trequired `
http.Server` hardening field (e.g. a future\n   617\t`MaxHeaderBytes` cap), upda
te `requiredHTTPServerFields` AND the\n   618\t`http.Server` construction in `cm
