        output='     1\t# Quota Usage Metrics\n     2\t\n     3\tYalla emits in-
process quota decision metrics through\n     4\t`telemetry.QuotaUsageMetrics`. T
he API process wires the quota checker to\n     5\t`telemetry.DefaultQuotaUsageM
etrics`, and `GET /metrics` returns the snapshot in\n     6\tthe standard `yalla
.output.v1` envelope under `data.quota_usage`.\n     7\t\n     8\tThe metric ser
ies are intentionally low cardinality:\n     9\t\n    10\t- `resource`: the clos
ed quota dimension, for example `projects`, `services`,\n    11\t  `domains`, or
`memory_mb`\n    12\t- `enforcement_mode`: `hard`, `soft`, `metered`, `disabled`
, `unknown`, or\n    13\t  `other`\n    14\t- `outcome`: `allowed`, `rejected`, 
or `error`\n    15\t- `reason`: a bounded reason such as `reserved`, `limit_exce
eded`,\n    16\t  `unconstrained`, `disabled`, `invalid_resource`, or `reservati
on_insert_failed`\n    17\t\n    18\tEach series also carries the latest `curren
t`, `reserved`, `requested`, and\n    19\t`limit` counts plus the latest `reques
t_id`, `correlation_id`,\n    20\t`organization_id`, `principal_id`, and `job_id
` observed for that series. Treat\n    21\tthose identifiers as log-join and sou
rce-row hints, not dashboard group-by\n    22\tlabels. Dashboards should group o
nly by the low-cardinality fields above.\n    23\t\n    24\tIncident workflow:\n
   25\t\n    26\t1. Look for `outcome=rejected` with `reason=limit_exceeded` to 
distinguish real\n    27\t   customer limit pressure from infrastructure failure
s.\n    28\t2. Compare `current + reserved + requested` against `limit` on the l
atest\n    29\t   sample to understand why a hard limit rejected the request.\n 
  30\t3. Look for `outcome=error` series to detect quota infrastructure failures
such\n    31\t   as lookup, usage-lock, reservation-sum, or reservation-insert f
ailures.\n    32\t4. Copy the latest `request_id`, `correlation_id`, or `job_id`
from the series\n    33\t   and search structured API or worker logs for the sam
e identifier.\n    34\t5. Use `organization_id` only to navigate tenant-scoped s
ource rows during an\n    35\t   incident. It is an operational hint, not a metr
ic label.\n    36\t\n    37\tQuota metrics do not record request bodies, API key
s, cookies, rendered\n    38\tenvironment variables, database URLs, Dokploy toke
ns, entitlement override\n    39\treasons, or error strings. Unknown resource na
mes and free-form reasons are\n    40\tcollapsed to bounded values before storag
