e hierarchy,\n   968\tstable ID prefixes, cursor-based pagination, common mutati
ng endpoint patterns,\n   969\tfrontend-specific error handling guidance, and fa
ilure recovery.\n   970\t\n   971\tThe guide preserves the production boundary: 
customers, agents, CI, and frontend\n   972\ttraffic all reach Dokploy only thro
ugh the Yalla API; Postgres remains the\n   973\tsource of truth; `yalla-worker`
