5\t\n   986\t## TLS Termination and Proxy Header Trust\n   987\t\n   988\tThe Ya
lla control-plane API binary (`cmd/yalla-api`) deliberately\n   989\tdoes NOT te
rminate TLS itself.\n   990\t**TLS is terminated at the operator's reverse proxy
**\n   991\t(ingress controller, load balancer, or front-door proxy), which\n   
992\tforwards the request to the API over an internal network. Keeping certifica
te material out of the API process\n   993\tnarrows the secret surface, leverage
s the proxy's vetted cipher\n   994\tsuite / HSTS / OCSP stapling defaults, and 
lets operators rotate\n   995\tcertificates without an API restart. The posture 
is pinned by\n   996\t`internal/release/http_server_hardening_static_test.go`; a
regression\n   997\tin any one of the following is caught at build time:\n   998
\t\n   999\t- **No in-process TLS.** The API binary MUST NOT call\n  1000\t  `Li
stenAndServeTLS` or `ServeTLS`, and the constructed\n  1001\t  `*http.Server` MU
ST NOT set `TLSConfig` or `TLSNextProto`. Any\n  1002\t  TLS-termination shape i
nside the binary is rejected.\n  1003\t- **Slowloris guard.** Every `*http.Serve
r` literal in the API\n  1004\t  binary MUST set a positive `ReadHeaderTimeout`.
The current value\n  1005\t  is `10 * time.Second`. Removing the field, or initi
alising the\n  1006\t  server with the zero value, is rejected.\n  1007\t- **Clo
sed-set proxy header trust.** The rate limiter resolves the\n  1008\t  caller's 
identity through `ClientIP(r)` in\n  1009\t  `internal/controlplane/httpapi/rate
limit.go`. The helper consults\n  1010\t  only two forwarding headers:\n  1011\t
 - `X-Forwarded-For` — the **first hop only** is taken so a forged\n  1012\t    
tail entry cannot displace the real client.\n  1013\t  - `X-Real-IP` as a fallba
ck.\n  1014\t  No other forwarded-* family header is honoured. RFC 7239\n  1015\
